You make a great point. Using a static "You are reviewing..." string for every step feels disjointed when the system is capable of dynamic, multi-level workflows (like Validation, Verification, and Approval).
Since we already capture the exact workflow stage from the database into a state variable called viewingBatchState when the modal opens, we can easily inject this into the subtitle.
Here is the exact fix for **VoucherAuthorization.js**.
### The Fix
Scroll down to where your "Universal Action Screen" begins (around line **1018** in your provided code).
**Find this block:**
```javascript
            {/* --- STATE 2: UNIVERSAL ACTION SCREEN --- */}
            {isActionMode && (
              <Box sx={jaStyles.actionScreenBox}>
                <Typography variant="h5" fontWeight="bold" gutterBottom>
                  Process Workflow Action
                </Typography>
                <Typography
                  variant="body1"
                  color="text.secondary"
                  textAlign="center"
                  sx={jaStyles.actionSubtitle}
                >
                  You are reviewing Batch <strong>{viewingBatchId}</strong>.
                  Please select your decision and provide remarks below.
                </Typography>

```
**Replace it completely with this:**
```javascript
            {/* --- STATE 2: UNIVERSAL ACTION SCREEN --- */}
            {isActionMode && (
              <Box sx={jaStyles.actionScreenBox}>
                <Typography variant="h5" fontWeight="bold" gutterBottom>
                  Process Workflow Action
                </Typography>
                <Typography
                  variant="body1"
                  color="text.secondary"
                  textAlign="center"
                  sx={jaStyles.actionSubtitle}
                >
                  You are currently processing the <strong>{viewingBatchState || "Review"}</strong> stage for Batch <strong>{viewingBatchId}</strong>.
                  Please select your decision and provide remarks below.
                </Typography>

```
### Why this works:
 * viewingBatchState pulls directly from the WORKFLOW_STAGE column in your Oracle WORKFLOW_TRANSITIONS table.
 * If the batch is at Step 1, it will say: *"You are currently processing the **Validation** stage..."*
 * If it is at Step 3, it will say: *"You are currently processing the **Final Approval** stage..."*
 * We included a fallback (|| "Review") just in case the stage name ever comes back null, so the UI doesn't break or look grammatically incorrect!
